WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.115 --> 00:00:14.987
"Detective Smith is missing," Roxy thought.

2
00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:18.881
"I have to get to police headquarters."

3
00:00:18.882 --> 00:00:22.183
She called to her friends. "Don't wait for me.

4
00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:31.183
I, um, dropped something!" Roxy ran off.

5
00:00:31.184 --> 00:00:34.901
The parking lot at police headquarters was empty.

6
00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:38.622
"Where are all the police cars?" Roxy said.

7
00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:44.976
"And where is everyone?"

8
00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:48.848
When she went inside, Roxy blinked in surprise.

9
00:00:48.849 --> 00:00:53.504
All the walls were crooked, and the floors were slanted.

10
00:00:53.505 --> 00:00:56.757
"What happened in here?" Roxy said.

11
00:00:56.758 --> 00:01:00.710
"It's like a fun house at an amusement park!"

12
00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:04.374
A hallway was lined with mirrors.

13
00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:07.775
One mirror made Roxy look tall and skinny.

14
00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:12.479
Another one made her head look enormous.

15
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.977
Roxy made her way to the break room.

16
00:01:14.978 --> 00:01:18.060
The coffeemaker was on, and cookies sat on the counter.

17
00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:21.707
Music played on a radio.

18
00:01:21.708 --> 00:01:24.230
But nobody was there.

19
00:01:24.231 --> 00:01:28.168
Roxy scratched her head. "This is odd."

20
00:01:28.169 --> 00:01:31.057
Click . . . Ba-doom!

21
00:01:31.058 --> 00:01:35.521
The floor tilted under Roxy's feet, and she slid down into darkness.

22
00:01:35.522 --> 00:01:38.681
"Oof!" Roxy landed on a hard floor.

23
00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:42.165
"Rocket Girl?" It was Detective Smith.

24
00:01:42.166 --> 00:01:46.676
Using her night vision, Roxy saw she was in a concrete room.

25
00:01:46.677 --> 00:01:48.498
The detective stood near her.

26
00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:51.542
Other police officers were in the room too.

27
00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:55.441
Roxy grinned. "Are you all playing hide-and-seek?"

28
00:01:55.442 --> 00:01:57.429
Detective Smith looked annoyed.

29
00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.065
"This isn't funny, Rocket Girl. We've been stuck down here since yesterday!"

30
00:02:02.066 --> 00:02:06.079
Roxy gulped. "Oh . . . Sorry to hear that.

31
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.307
What happened to the building? It's like a fun house."

32
00:02:10.308 --> 00:02:15.162
"We hired a builder to make some improvements." Detective Smith sighed.

33
00:02:15.163 --> 00:02:17.402
"Obviously he did a terrible job.

34
00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.872
We can't even use the building now."

35
00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.855
"Who is the builder?" Roxy asked.

36
00:02:22.856 --> 00:02:26.219
"His name is Jack Hammer," Detective Smith said.

37
00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.297
"We won't hire him again."

38
00:02:28.298 --> 00:02:30.621
Another police officer walked over.

39
00:02:30.622 --> 00:02:34.410
"How will we get out of here?" she asked.

40
00:02:34.411 --> 00:02:38.165
Roxy laughed. "That's easy."

41
00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:45.339
She flew the police officers up to the break room.

42
00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.778
Detective Smith grabbed a cookie and took a bite.

43
00:02:48.779 --> 00:02:52.164
The police dispatcher saw a light flashing on the phone.

44
00:02:52.165 --> 00:02:55.670
"Yikes!" she said. "We have messages."

45
00:02:55.671 --> 00:02:58.190
She played the first message.

46
00:02:58.191 --> 00:03:01.922
"Hello? I'm worried about my friends Brenda and Dan Dooley.

47
00:03:01.923 --> 00:03:03.865
They moved into their new house yesterday.

48
00:03:03.866 --> 00:03:05.661
It's at Ten Puddle Lane.

49
00:03:05.662 --> 00:03:10.692
I tried calling and knocking on their door, but there's no answer."

50
00:03:10.693 --> 00:03:13.803
Other people had called with similar messages.

51
00:03:13.804 --> 00:03:16.608
Many of them had called more than once.

52
00:03:16.609 --> 00:03:24.012
Detective Smith swallowed the last bite of his cookie. "Oh boy."
